    "title": "pandas.Index.nunique — pandas 2.0.3 documentation",
    "status": 200,
    "markdown": "# pandas.Index.nunique#\n\n- \nIndex.nunique(*dropna=True* )[source]#\n- Return number of unique elements in the object. Excludes NA values by default. \n  - Parameters\n    - **dropna** bool, default True\n    - Don’t include NaN in the count.\n  - Returns\n    - int\n See also \n  - `DataFrame.nunique`\n  - Method nunique for DataFrame.\n  - `Series.count`\n  - Count non-NA/null observations in the Series.\n Examples >>> s = pd.Series([1, 3, 5, 7, 7]) >>> s 0 1 1 3 2 5 3 7 4 7 dtype: int64 >>> s.nunique() 4",
